Notes, none of which is a failed row
------------------------------------
- Row 7, second sub-case: after a bare-strip pick on a day that carries records the centre
  shows that day's record (readout and highlight agree) but no marker is accent-coloured.
  That is the row's own wording — the strip picked the day, not a record — and it is what the
  page does; recorded here so nobody reads the nuance as a hidden pass.
- At the year scale (outside the ±2-year month window) a year is a few pixels wide, so markers
  of different days in the same year can sit within a marker width of each other (e.g.
  2016-09-14 and 2016-09-20 both centre near x 425). The documents already record this as
  "What is still missing"; it does not change the marker count or the day each marker carries.
- This run counts 49 month ticks from 2024-11 (the round-2 log in the tree says 48 from
  2024-12). The live measurement here is the one above: 49 .tick.m whose _date values enumerate
  every month from 2024-11 to 2028-11 with no gaps or repeats, and TL.winFrom/winTo =
  2024-11-01 / 2028-11-30.
